<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plombières Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1858</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-italian-war-of-independence">Second Italian War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Plombières Agreement was a secret understanding reached on 21 July 1858 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camillo-benso-count-of-cavour">Cavour</a> at the spa town of Plombières-les-Bains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. France promised to help the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> in a war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> provoked by Austria, in return for Savoy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a>, and a marriage was arranged between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a>'s daughter Clotilde and Prince Napoléon. It led to the war of 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plombieres-agreement.jpg" alt="Plombières Agreement" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gigillo83 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italia_1843.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
